(7548325, 1209001, 173844, '<td valign="top">The title nails it for me --  the endless wilderness, rugged and forbidding, and the road one must take.  Lines wander every which way, adding complexity to the task.  The colors are muted, but they''re very compelling in support of the overall mood.  The depth of field is spectacular, passing right through the middle of the image.  The square crop assists in leading the eye into rather than out.  Lot of detail and sharpness, the sharpness even being overdone to the extent that white lines hug the mountain edges.<br/>Personal favorite of the challenge.</td>', 'The title nails it for me --  the endless wilderness, rugged and forbidding, and the road one must take.  Lines wander every which way, adding complexity to the task.  The colors are muted, but they''re very compelling in support of the overall mood.  The depth of field is spectacular, passing right through the middle of the image.  The square crop assists in leading the eye into rather than out.  Lot of detail and sharpness, the sharpness even being overdone to the extent that white lines hug the mountain edges.Personal favorite of the challenge.', '2017-12-14 12:44:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(7548333, 1209072, 173844, '<td valign="top">What a fine, fine image.  The grass and its reflections are both inviting and decoratively splendid, whether enjoyed as nature''s endless inventiveness and beauty or as pure abstract. The water, its ripples and colors, is a delightful background no less becoming than the grasses.  Truly enchanting.<br/>I spent a pleasant 9 minutes listening to the title song by Yes, and can only surmise that it holds meaning for the artist (aside from the fish on the left).</td>', 'What a fine, fine image.  The grass and its reflections are both inviting and decoratively splendid, whether enjoyed as nature''s endless inventiveness and beauty or as pure abstract. The water, its ripples and colors, is a delightful background no less becoming than the grasses.  Truly enchanting.I spent a pleasant 9 minutes listening to the title song by Yes, and can only surmise that it holds meaning for the artist (aside from the fish on the left).', '2017-12-14 13:14:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7548339, 1209075, 173844, '<td valign="top">When this image popped up I thought, hold it a second, this is wonderful.  In other words, hardly just a peek through the venetians.  I''ll go backwards --  the incredible vignette, the sun blasting through the rain-spattered window and the blinds harvesting the beautiful purples and oranges.  I''m not sure the flags add anything additional to the image, but there they are.  So much from, ostensibly, so little.  Works really well with the square crop.  Breathtaking.<br/>Another personal favorite, along with "Road to Mordor."</td>', 'When this image popped up I thought, hold it a second, this is wonderful.  In other words, hardly just a peek through the venetians.  I''ll go backwards --  the incredible vignette, the sun blasting through the rain-spattered window and the blinds harvesting the beautiful purples and oranges.  I''m not sure the flags add anything additional to the image, but there they are.  So much from, ostensibly, so little.  Works really well with the square crop.  Breathtaking.Another personal favorite, along with "Road to Mordor."', '2017-12-14 13:31:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7548340, 1208857, 173844, '<td valign="top">Delightful.  It''s such a fun and uplifting image.  I love these women and the girl, quirky originals.  The rain is no match for them.  The square crop well suits the moment in time.  I will enjoy looking at this again and again, so into my favorites it goes.</td>', 'Delightful.  It''s such a fun and uplifting image.  I love these women and the girl, quirky originals.  The rain is no match for them.  The square crop well suits the moment in time.  I will enjoy looking at this again and again, so into my favorites it goes.', '2017-12-14 13:46:06.000000', NULL, 1),
